and the consequences for downstream implementation work.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A decision record exists that names exactly one topology to productize first,\n52\t  with the alternative explicitly deferred or rejected.\n53\t- Each supportability criterion is evaluated for both topologies with evidence\n54\t  (upstream documentation, behavior observed in evaluation, known issues).\n55\t- The consequences for the Platform Operator integration and the Dashboard\n56\t  integration are recorded in the decision record.\n57\t- The decision has been reviewed and accepted by the owning stakeholders.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-1 (gating): the topology decision is a prerequisite for the productization\n62\t  approach delivering HLR-1; it does not itself implement HLR-1 scope.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a52dcdd4a6379b37","agent_id":"aeb1829f2f10afebf","session_id":"51e94c62-f637-4718-aadc-0000f673a195","uuid":"a24e7571-2dbb-46ca-b89b-d72ece7f3753","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:25:51.693Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92ff96fd46ac7300","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
