50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A scan report exists covering Feast and the complete transitive dependency\n53\t  tree of every artifact type to be shipped.\n54\t- Every flagged license has a recorded disposition (approved, remediated, or\n55\t  blocking).\n56\t- Any required remediation is documented with its downstream impact.\n57\t- A recorded go/no-go decision exists for use of the Feast SDK in a supported\n58\t  workbench image.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1: license-clear dependencies are a precondition for productized,\n63\t  supported images.\n64\t- HLR-2 (gating): the workbench SDK preinstall requires the license go/no-go.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a52dcdd4a6379b37","agent_id":"aeb1829f2f10afebf","session_id":"51e94c62-f637-4718-aadc-0000f673a195","uuid":"d543d78b-5039-43de-a117-c4bf640d4eed","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:25:56.689Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-97ec977b473fdd1a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
