orted limits**: the supported deployment topology and its limits;\n56\t  customer-managed (bring-your-own) offline store requirement, since managed\n57\t  offline-store infrastructure is out of scope; any topology-specific\n58\t  restrictions identified during implementation.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Documentation covers all three required topics: enablement, getting-started\n63\t  walkthrough, and supported limits.\n64\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented Feature Store\n65\t  (enablement flow, workbench SDK path, and selected topology) and reflects\n66\t  actual behavior.\n67\t- The bring-your-own offline-store limitation is stated explicitly.\n68\t- The documentation is published in the RHOAI documentation set.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4: product documentation covers enablement, a getting-started\n73\t  walkthrough, and supported limits.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a52dcdd4a6379b37","agent_id":"aeb1829f2f10afebf","session_id":"51e94c62-f637-4718-aadc-0000f673a195","uuid":"a3630c49-95c3-4022-9d2d-61323c205a00","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:26:08.346Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99c1b843ac32bc6d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
