erence (2/2)\n32\tEvery edge in the summary diagram matches the target epic's frontmatter `dependencies`, and vice versa (verified edge-by-edge for all 11 main-plan edges and all 6 branch edges); arrow direction is dependency → dependent. No cycles; no edges to nonexistent epics. Rule-mandated parallelism verified pair-by-pair: E002 ∥ E003 (rule 7), no E003 → E004 edge (rule 8), and E004 (konflux-onboarding) has no blocking edge in either direction with any general implementation — E005, E006, E007, and both branch epics — with coupling correctly enforced via \"build pipeline green\" / pinned-digest ACs (rule 10 / rule 13). The E005 image-digest relationship to the branch deployment is correctly an AC gate, not a `dependencies` edge. Branch files both set `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001`, which appears in their direct `dependencies`; no main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its `dependencies`, and E005/E007 correctly point at the Investigation. Rule 11 edges (E002–E007 → E008) are present and complete. Critical path (3) is reasonable for this strategy size given the deliberately parallel structure. One observation, not a DAG defect: E006's verification AC needs \"a feature store endpoint,\" which no epic in E006's dependency set produces — see Criterion 6.\n33\t\n34\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n35\tEvery epic has a single component/team tuple, all canonical (`Feature Store`, `Platform Operator`, `Notebooks`, `Dashboard`, `Documentation` — all present in `.context/rhai-components.txt`; validator confirmed). The non-obvious `Notebooks` mapping for HLR-2 is explicitly justified in the summary's Component Mapping section. No scope duplication: E005 (operator enablement), the branch epics (deployment packaging), and E007 (Dashboard surface) are distinct deliverables with no rebuilt shared surface. No work-product type mixing — docs authoring is isolated in E008. No epic exceeds sprint scale. Team inferences (strategy has no Impacted Teams table) are flagged in Health Warnings rather than silently asserted.\n36\t\n37\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n38\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome selects which branch epic exists and rewrites E005/E007 integration shapes, with two bounded branch files covering both outcomes. All Implementation epics produce concrete artifacts (repository, scan report, Konflux application, operator integration, workbench image, Dashboard surface, docs, deployment packaging). Gating metadata is complete and correct: E005 and E007 have `gated_by: E001` (present in their direct `dependencies`) with `action: rewrite` and populated `fallback_approach`; both branch epics have `gated_by: E001` with `action: remove` and fallback. No epic lists an Investigation in `dependencies` without `gated_by`. E006's dependency on E003 (license-validation, an Implementation) is a scheduling dependency and correctly carries no gate.\n39\t\n40\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n41\tSignal fields are type-appropriate everywhere: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all eight Implementation epics (including both branches) carry `ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`. Rationales match frontmatter values and check out against the workspace: E007's `architecture_claims: 1` is supported by the Dashboard architecture context file (the only one present, documenting CR reads and per-component feature flags); E005's `architecture_claims: 0` correctly reflects that Platform Operator has no architecture context file; Feature Store is correctly treated as a new component throughout. E005/E007 `open_questions: -1` correctly reflect the unresolved topology question that gates them, while E002/E004/E006 correctly score `1` since topology does not change their approach. E001's investigation signals are consistent with its own ACs (stakeholder sign-off → `human_judgment_required: -1`). E003/E004's `external_dependency: 0` values are borderline