{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32b632dd99a4f35","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Decide the Feast deployment topology to productize first\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide the Feast deployment topology to productize first\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis Investigation resolves the strategy's open question: which Feast deployment\n30\ttopology to productize first — the operator-based deployment or the standalone\n31\tserver per project. Upstream Feast supports both, but their supportability\n32\tprofiles differ. The outcome determines the shape of the Feast deployment\n33\tproductization, the Platform Operator enablement mechanism, and the Dashboard\n34\tendpoint surface, so it must be settled before those implementations are\n35\tfinalized.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Evaluate both upstream-supported deployment topologies against supportability\n40\t  criteria: per-project isolation, upgrade and rollback behavior, operational\n41\t  load of the platform, failure modes, and support boundaries.\n42\t- Assess how each topology fits the existing managed-component enablement model\n43\t  of the Platform Operator.\n44\t- Assess what per-project endpoint discovery would look like under each topology\n45\t  for Dashboard integration.\n46\t- Produce a decision record naming the selected topology, the supporting\n47\t  evidence, and the consequences for downstream implementation work.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A decision record exists that names exactly one topology to productize first,\n52\t  with the alternative explicitly deferred or rejected.\n53\t- Each supportability criterion is evaluated for both topologies with evidence\n54\t  (upstream documentation, behavior observed in evaluation, known issues).\n55\t- The consequences for the Platform Operator integration and the Dashboard\n56\t  integration are recorded in the decision record.\n57\t- The decision has been reviewed and accepted by the owning stakeholders.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-1 (gating): the topology decision is a prerequisite for the productization\n62\t  approach delivering HLR-1; it does not itself implement HLR-1 scope.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3868c449c31b27c","agent_id":"a954cbc11de1413ef","session_id":"51e94c62-f637-4718-aadc-0000f673a195","uuid":"a650c7e6-79c0-429d-9a5e-92596fe6ca82","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:32:21.004Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b32b632dd99a4f35","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 after revision"}
