e reference implementation.\n52\t- Cover per-project (namespace) isolation and lifecycle (create, upgrade,\n53\t  remove) for each project's server as specified by the topology decision\n54\t  record.\n55\t- Ensure each project's server endpoints are discoverable for platform\n56\t  integration (operator enablement and Dashboard link-out).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A standalone Feast server can be deployed per project from the productized\n61\t  packaging in the midstream repository.\n62\t- Servers in different projects are isolated from each other as specified in\n63\t  the topology decision record.\n64\t- Per-project server lifecycle (create, upgrade, remove) completes successfully.\n65\t- The productized images build green in the platform build pipeline.\n66\t- The per-project endpoints the deployment exposes are documented for the\n67\t  Platform Operator and Dashboard integrations.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1: the supported, installable Feature Store with productized images,\n72\t  delivered via the standalone per-project server topology.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3868c449c31b27c","agent_id":"a954cbc11de1413ef","session_id":"51e94c62-f637-4718-aadc-0000f673a195","uuid":"9fed9cd5-aa18-4aad-916c-6aca48a66375","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:32:37.272Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88acfbea665c7d76","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9006 after revision"}
