eferenced epics exist. Every edge in both mermaid\ndiagrams matches the target epic's frontmatter `dependencies` exactly, and vice\nversa (verified edge-by-edge for all 8 main-plan and 6 branch edges). Arrows point\ndependency → dependent as required. Rule-mandated parallelism is respected:\n- Rule 7/8: E002 ∥ E003 (both roots), and no E003 → E002/E004 edge.\n- Rule 10: E004 (konflux-onboarding) has edges only from E002 and to E008 (Rule 11\n  docs-last). Checked against every general-implementation epic — E005, E006, E007,\n  BRANCH-A-E009, BRANCH-B-E009 — no edge in either direction; coupling is enforced\n  by \"build pipeline green\" ACs on E004 and both branch epics, as required.\n- Rule 13 exception correctly applied: E005's pinned image digests (produced by the\n  branch deployment + Konflux) are an AC gate (\"Image references resolve to pinned,\n  productized image digests\"), not a `dependencies` edge.\n- Conditional branches: both branch files set `branch` (A/B, matching filenames) and\n  `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001`; no main-plan epic lists a branch epic in its\n  `dependencies` — E005 and E007 correctly gate on the Investigation itself.\nCritical path is 3 (e.g., E002 → E004 → E008), slightly below the 4-5 heuristic for\nan M new-component strategy, but this reflects genuinely rule-correct parallelism\n(onboarding chain and cross-repo integration work are independent), not a missing\nedge — every Rule 11 docs-last edge from all six main-plan implementations is\npresent.\n\nMinor: E006's scope requires an SDK version \"compatible with the productized\nFeature Store\" — a version established by E002's pinned import. The no-edge\ntreatment is right (configuration reference, AC-gated by the pinned-version AC),\nbut the DAG Justification table justifies E006 ∥ E005/E007 and never addresses the\nE006 ∥ E002 relationship.\n\nMinor: the branch DAG diagram labels the license-validation node \"E03\" (should be\n\"E003\") — a label typo only; the node ID and all edges are correct.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\nEvery epic has a single canonical component/team tuple, all copied from\n`.context/rhai-components.txt` (Feature Store, Platform Operator, Notebooks,\nDashboard, Documentation — all verified canonical). The non-obvious Notebooks\nmapping for the workbench SDK epic is documented and correct. No epic spans\nmultiple teams. The two branch epics build alternative deployments of the same\nsurface but are mutually exclusive by gate (`action=remove` on both), so they are\nnot scope duplication. No work-product type mixing: the docs epic (E008) is pure\ncontent authoring with no code scope. Epic sizes are within ~2 weeks.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome selects which branch epic exists and\nrewrites E005's and E007's integration approach — it changes downstream structure,\nand it has downstream dependents. All Implementation epics produce concrete\nartifacts (repository, scan report, pipeline config, operator integration, image,\nDashboard UI, published docs). Gating metadata is complete and correct: E005, E007,\nand both branch epics set `gated_by` with `gate_failure_impact` populated (action +\nfallback_approach) and the `gated_by` target (E001) in each epic's direct\n`dependencies`. Every epic listing the Investigation in `dependencies` also sets\n`gated_by`. No scheduling dependency is misfiled as a gate.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nSignal fields are type-correct: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal\nrubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all Implementation epics and branch epics carry\n`ai_signals` with `investigation_signals: null`. Signal values are consistent with\nthe strategy content: E005 and E007 correctly score `open_questions: -1` (the\ntopology question changes their approach), while E002/E003/E004/E006 correctly\nscore `open_questions: 1` with rationales explaining topology-independence — the\ntrap of scoring 1 despite the unresolved question was avoided. E007's\n`architecture_claims: 1` is verified: the Dashboard architecture context file\nexists and documents the CR-read/per-component-feature-flag enablement pattern;\nE005's `architecture_claims: 0` is likewise correct (no Platform Operator\narchitecture context file exists). Rationales in all ten ai-signals files match the\nfrontmatter values. Arithmetic/thresholds not checked per instructions.\n\nMinor: E004's `external_dependency: 0` is borderline — its rationale names only\ninternal build-team coordination (\"no upstream contribution needed\"), which is\narguably not an external (upstream/vendor) dependency; value 1 would also fit.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs are\npresent wherever applicable: build-pipeline-green on E004 (\"A build completes green\nend-to-end\") and on both branch epics (\"The productized images build green in the\nplatform build pipeline\"); docs technical review on E008 (\"technically reviewed\nagainst the implemented Feature Store\"); pinned productized digests on E005; clean\nteardown/disable on E005 and lifecycle (create/upgrade/remove) on branch B. No\nreplacement epics exist (new component), so the rollback/feature-flag AC rule does\nnot bind, though E005 and branch A cover disable/upgrade paths anyway. No soft ACs\n(schedule/timing constraints) were found — E001's stakeholder-acceptance AC is\ntestable. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe full strategy scope is covered: operator enablement with productized images\n(HLR-1 via onboarding chain + E005 + branch), workbench SDK (HLR-2 via E006),\nDashboard presence and endpoint links (HLR-3 via E007), and documentation (HLR-4\nvia E008). The strategy's single open question is covered by exactly two bounded\nbranches matching the two upstream-supported topologies — no outcome is\nunaccounted for. Out-of-scope boundaries are carried forward